  "term": "rheumatoid arthritis",
  "definition": "Rheumatoid arthritis is a long-lasting autoimmune disease that affects the whole body, causing ongoing inflammation of the joint lining, worsening joint damage, and problems outside the joints. It can limit physical functioning and lower quality of life.",
